  "description": "FAWLEW crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4 n c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H112 Cu8 Gd4 N8 O32 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),0.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1C (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1C (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2A (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2C (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2B (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.175-3.999 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.26-111.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Cu8(OH)8(L)8(O2CCHMe2)8](ClO4)4·0.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III), Cu(II).",
